This is a quick port for OS4 of the SDL action game 'Njam' v1.21 
by author Milan Babuskov.

OS4 port by Sharakmir (Kjell Breding).

Njam URL: http://njam.sourceforge.net/ (where you can find a lot of info!)

Njam is fast-paced cross-platform pacman-like game written in C++ using SDL 
library. It has network duel support and a lot of nice features. More info 
about this game is found in the enclosed documentation (in the html drawer).


RUNNING THE GAME - OS4

Just open a shell and type 'Njam_OS4' to get started. You can also start 
by clicking the game icon which starts the game in a full screen mode. 
If you want to play in window mode, start the game with 'njam_OS4 -w'.

A small issue: when entering the 'join network duel' in the main menu, 
it's not possible to type '.' when entering an ip address. To enter a 
ip address, edit njam.conf and type in the correct server ip address. 
E.g.:

I=192.198.0.100 (I've set this address as default in njam.conf, feel 
free to change it to whatever works for you).

This address is then used everytime you play the game. In case your 
opponents server ip changes, just edit njam.conf again.


